    <div class="pg-eb">Meet the founder</div>
    <h2 id="ab-fh">Nimisha Nailor</h2>
    <p>Nimisha lived with chronic inflammation and PCOS. Along the way she found something that helped her recovery: goat dairy.</p>
    <p>What she couldn’t find was a goat whey protein she genuinely wanted to have every day. One that was clean, great-tasting and fairly priced. Nothing like it existed.</p>
    <p class="ab-big">So she made it.</p>
    <div class="ab-sig"><b>Nimisha Nailor</b><small>Founder, Kultra</small></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="ab-s ab-w" aria-labelledby="ab-wh"><div class="ab-in ab-c ab-r">
  <div class="pg-eb">Who it’s for</div>
  <h2 id="ab-wh">For people the usual protein aisle forgot.</h2>
  <p>Kultra is made for people managing insulin resistance, gut sensitivity or chronic inflammation, and for anyone who has found mainstream protein powders a poor fit.</p>
  <p>Goat milk is naturally A2, and goat whey is naturally lower in lactose than typical cow whey. For many people, that makes it a gentler place to start.</p>
</div></section>

